WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:11.519
So to cover the optimization philosophy briefly, we want to be thinking about optimization throughout the entire project

2
00:00:11.519 --> 00:00:17.440
It's no good starting a project and throwing all the content in and then getting towards the end of the project

3
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.500
Say you're at the last 90% and then figuring out how you need to optimize it

4
00:00:20.559 --> 00:00:24.940
You need to almost optimize on the go and also when starting your project

5
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:30.079
Figure out the the target platforms target frame rates that you want to be hitting

6
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.039
Ahead of time and it allows you to make some

7
00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:40.020
Optimizations on the way and then also throughout this course, we'll be talking about just good content pipelines

8
00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:44.219
You can follow with your your content whether it be on the mesh side the material side

9
00:00:44.859 --> 00:00:50.399
Whatever it might be. You can be making these optimizations as you go on ensuring your project is hitting

10
00:00:51.039 --> 00:00:53.200
Framerate, so you really want to be talking about

11
00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:56.799
optimization throughout the entire length of the project and

12
00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:02.240
Constantly putting checks in place to ensure you're hitting the target frame rate on the desired platform
